  "summary_md": "Renewables, gold, RVs, and packaging fill today’s list, but the unifying thread is a sharp divergence between companies converting tangible tailwinds into execution and those riding speculative repositioning. Gold developers CTGO, IDR, and PZG are translating elevated prices into permitting advances, production momentum, and collapsing short interest, while USAU and VGZ remain betwixt asset potential and market skepticism. In recreational vehicles, MCFT’s planned merger with MPX headlines a consolidation push, just as VEEE abandons its marine business entirely via a reverse merger into a Greenland mineral venture.\n\nThe most distinctive stories sit at the extremes: BESS is executing a textbook originate‑develop‑rotate model in utility-scale storage, and STEM’s software pivot is printing record margins and positive adjusted EBITDA. On the other side, NRGV’s core operations still burn cash at deeply negative margins, NXXT pairs rapid AI‑fuel‑delivery growth with insider selling and persistent losses, and ORBS plays a unique treasury‑wrapper game tied to OpenAI and crypto sentiment. RV names MBUU and WGO are running disciplined channel strategies but face a gradual demand recovery that is testing market patience.",
